    "authorAssociation": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.statusline\n\n### Question\n\nI don't know if it's me, but I think the cursor line location next to the cursor column location changed. It does not behave like the column location. When there is only 1 digit there is no space added.\r\n\r\n![image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/edbae5a5-5945-4371-9284-b236e1e1b483)\r\n![image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/c11e5e0a-822b-4947-8d9b-98fd923790d4)\r\n\r\nI don't know if it was always like that or if I'm just starting to slowly go insane :D",
    "bodyHTML": "<h3 dir=\"auto\">Contributing guidelines</h3>\n<ul class=\"contains-task-list\">\n<li class=\"task-list-item\"><input type=\"checkbox\" id=\"\" disabled=\"\" class=\"task-list-item-checkbox\" aria-label=\"Completed task\" checked=\"\"> I have read <a href=\"https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md\">CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md</a></li>\n</ul>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Module(s)</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">mini.statusline</p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Question</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">I don't know if it's me, but I think the cursor line location next to the cursor column location changed. It does not behave like the column location. When there is only 1 digit there is no space added.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" href=\"https://private-user-images.githubusercontent.com/93912163/417607530-edbae5a5-5945-4371-9284-b236e1e1b483.png?jwt=eyJ0eXAiOiJKV1QiLCJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiJ9..QmrsN8tBMKYos2QcXQN0l50OJO8iOLjZcMSBcPNwlHo\"><img src=\"https://private-user-images.githubusercontent.com/93912163/417607530-edbae5a5-5945-4371-9284-b236e1e1b483.png?jwt=eyJ0eXAiOiJKV1QiLCJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiJ9..QmrsN8tBMKYos2QcXQN0l50OJO8iOLjZcMSBcPNwlHo\" alt=\"image\" style=\"max-width: 100%;\"></a><br>\n<a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" href=\"https://private-user-images.githubusercontent.com/93912163/417607663-c11e5e0a-822b-4947-8d9b-98fd923790d4.png?jwt=eyJ0eXAiOiJKV1QiLCJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiJ9.._qdj7u4P2JBcAuimEiHeswfck29-Ev_q1yELhnr3h1g\"><img src=\"https://private-user-images.githubusercontent.com/93912163/417607663-c11e5e0a-822b-4947-8d9b-98fd923790d4.png?jwt=eyJ0eXAiOiJKV1QiLCJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiJ9.._qdj7u4P2JBcAuimEiHeswfck29-Ev_q1yELhnr3h1g\" alt=\"image\" style=\"max-width: 100%;\"></a></p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">I don't know if it was always like that or if I'm just starting to slowly go insane :D</p>",
    "bodyText": "Contributing guidelines\n\n I have read CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md\n\nModule(s)\nmini.statusline\nQuestion\nI don't know if it's me, but I think the cursor line location next to the cursor column location changed. It does not behave like the column location. When there is only 1 digit there is no space added.\n\n\nI don't know if it was always like that or if I'm just starting to slowly go insane :D",
    "category": {
        "createdAt": "2022-01-02T14:24:09Z",
        "description": "Ask the community for help",
        "emoji": ":pray:",
        "emojiHTML": "<div>🙏</div>",
        "id": "DIC_kwDOFoksYM4CAgqN",
        "isAnswerable": true,
        "name": "Q&A",
        "slug": "q-a",
        "updatedAt": "2022-01-02T14:24:09Z"
    },
    "closed": true,
    "closedAt": "2025-02-27T13:54:00Z",
    "comment_count": 1,
    "comment_data": [
        {
            "author": {
                "avatarUrl": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/24854248?u=d09fd974c6720eba3039db6beb2f1c1efecdb51d&v=4",
                "login": "echasnovski",
                "resourcePath": "/echasnovski",
                "url": "https://github.com/echasnovski"
            },
            "authorAssociation": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Do you mean that it is ` 0|1│ 1|0  ` and not `  0|1 │ 1|0  `?\r\n\r\nIt was [like that](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/e554890210cd29d017d6a0c1b1a46f995dcf9e64/lua/mini/statusline.lua#L434-L435) since the initial release around 40 months ago. It is mostly to reduce visually shifting sections while typing (and crossing the tenth column mark): the cursor column is thus `%2v` (padded to have width 2) and the same is done for total number of columns for symmetry. Maybe should have been like that for line numbers also, but decided to save width. Plus it visually separates lines and columns which can be a good thing.",
            "bodyHTML": "<p dir=\"auto\">Do you mean that it is <code class=\"notranslate\">0|1│ 1|0 </code> and not <code class=\"notranslate\"> 0|1 │ 1|0 </code>?</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">It was <a href=\"https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/e554890210cd29d017d6a0c1b1a46f995dcf9e64/lua/mini/statusline.lua#L434-L435\">like that</a> since the initial release around 40 months ago. It is mostly to reduce visually shifting sections while typing (and crossing the tenth column mark): the cursor column is thus <code class=\"notranslate\">%2v</code> (padded to have width 2) and the same is done for total number of columns for symmetry. Maybe should have been like that for line numbers also, but decided to save width. Plus it visually separates lines and columns which can be a good thing.</p>",
            "bodyText": "Do you mean that it is 0|1│ 1|0  and not  0|1 │ 1|0 ?\nIt was like that since the initial release around 40 months ago. It is mostly to reduce visually shifting sections while typing (and crossing the tenth column mark): the cursor column is thus %2v (padded to have width 2) and the same is done for total number of columns for symmetry. Maybe should have been like that for line numbers also, but decided to save width. Plus it visually separates lines and columns which can be a good thing.",
